      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head center max-60" style="margin-inline:auto"><p class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center">FAQs</p><h2>Pressure washing questions</h2></div>
        <div class="faq">
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q1">What is pressure washing?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q1"><div>Pressure washing cleans surfaces using a high-pressure water spray. It's a highly effective way to remove dirt, grime, mould, mildew and other build-up from surfaces like driveways, paths, patios, decks and walls.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q2">How does pressure washing work?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q2"><div>Pressure washers use a motor or engine to pump water at high pressure through a hose and nozzle. The high-pressure stream agitates and dislodges dirt and grime from the surface being cleaned.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q3">What surfaces can be pressure washed?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q3"><div>Pressure washing suits many surfaces, including concrete, brick, wood, vinyl, metal and some types of stone. We match the pressure and nozzle to each surface — and switch to soft washing for delicate areas — so we clean thoroughly without causing damage.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q4">Can you pressure wash when it's raining?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q4"><div>In most cases, yes. Unless there's a big storm or torrential rain, we can carry out most pressure washing jobs in the rain, and it doesn't affect the quality of the finished result.</div></div></div>
          <div class="faq__item"><button class="faq__q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q5">Can you remove oil stains and moss?<svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></button><div class="faq__a" id="q5"><div>In most cases, yes. We pre-treat oil, moss, lichen and algae before washing. Long-standing stains may lighten rather than vanish completely — we'll set honest expectations when we quote.</div></div></div>
